      "id": "claim_377a4215e8b341e19627634dee78dd5d",
      "statement": "Most mutable, non-catalog models implement a get_owner_id() method that resolves to the owning user (directly or by delegating through parent relationships, e.g. Module.get_owner_id returns self.course.owner_id), and backend/api/authorization.py uses this uniform OwnedResource protocol in validate_ownership/validate_owner_or_superadmin to authorize writes without each router re-deriving the owning user.",
